  "articleBody": "Installing D-shaped cabinet handles can seem like a straightforward task, but sometimes, a professional touch is exactly what you need to avoid headaches and ensure a perfect finish. So, when should you pick up the phone and call in an expert? \n\n*   **Uneven Cabinetry:** If your cabinet doors or drawer fronts aren't perfectly uniform or level, getting handles to look straight and consistent can be a real challenge. Pros have the tricks to compensate for these variances.\n*   **Matching Across a Full Kitchen:** Installing dozens of handles that all need to be precisely aligned can be incredibly time-consuming and frustrating. A professional can ensure every handle in your entire kitchen matches up flawlessly.\n*   **Repairing Existing Holes:** If you're replacing handles and the new ones don't match the old screw holes, you'll need careful repair and filler work. This takes skill to make sure the patches are invisible and the new holes are precisely drilled.\n*   **Avoiding Costly Mistakes:** Misdrilled holes are incredibly difficult to conceal and can permanently damage your finished cabinetry, potentially leading to expensive door or drawer replacement. If you want to avoid this risk, especially on high-end cabinets, bringing in an expert is a smart move. \n\nHH Remodeling LLC specializes in detailed interior finish work and can handle all your cabinet hardware installation needs, ensuring a perfect, worry-free result for your home in the Denver area.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
